        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://roadsidethoughts.com/ut/woodland-hills-xx-utah-profile.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Woodland Hills upgraded from town to city status on November 3, 2000, to gain greater administrative autonomy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodland_hills_utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Woodland Hills spans rugged terrain with elevations ranging from 5,000 feet to over 6,200 feet in the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodland_hills_utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Forested slopes of maple, aspen, oak, fir, and spruce in Woodland Hills support wildlife like elk, bears, and mountain lions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodland_hills_utah"
    },
    {
